<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Smurfit H1 pretax profit drops 37 pct.</title>
<headline>Smurfit H1 pretax profit drops 37 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>					  (million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		8.2		    vs 12.8</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.5		    vs 1.4</p>
<p> Pretax		     126.15		 vs 200.63</p>
<p> Turnover		   1,352.37	     vs 1,544.35</p>
<p> Operating profit	 113.41		 vs 164.90</p>
<p> Interest paid	    59.12		  vs 56.78</p>
<p> Interest received	29.13		  vs 32.01</p>
<p> Tax			  36.69		  vs 56.31</p>
<p> Net taxed		  89.47		  vs 144.32</p>
<p> Attributable	     86.69		  vs 137.82</p>
<p> Record date	    September 17, 1996</p>
<p> Pay date		 November 1, 1996</p>
<p> Ex-dividend date     September 9, 1996</p>
<p>NOTE - Paper and packaging group Jefferson Smurfit Plc said all regions suffered during the period from price reductions compared to the previous year.</p>
<p>-- Dublin newsroom 353 1 660 3377</p>
</text>
